  "answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative aimed at enhancing security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole. The project kicked off in July 2023 and has successfully completed its design and testing phases, with a prototype for secure file sharing tested ahead of schedule. The team is now moving into the development phase, led by Omar Jensen, with a focus on user interface enhancements starting in October. To support this, the executive board approved a total budget of $2 million, with specific allocations including $15,000 for training programs. The project team is expanding with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, who will be onboarded on September 10th. Additionally, the team is exploring partnership opportunities with TechInnovate for AI technology integration. A milestone celebration is scheduled for October 10th."
